-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Oct 24 04:54:57 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.31.0:
  * Stabilize model-package and EPContext data APIs in C and C++,
    with EPContext callback support across language bindings.
  * Cut CPU session-init overhead via parallel weight prepacking and
    faster quantized MoE experts (MLAS QNBit kernels); fused CPU
    LinearAttention and FP16 LayerNorm/RMSNorm acceleration.
  * Add Arm KleidiAI SVE2.1 FP16 GEMM and more RISC-V vector kernels.
  * Enable CoreML device-based execution-provider selection.
  * Harden model loading, graph partitioning and tensor validation.
  * GatherBlockQuantized with out-of-range indices now yields zero
    slices instead of following Gather error semantics.
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list.
- Bundled onnx stays at 1.22.0, which is not affected by
  CVE-2026-44512 (boo#1271019).
- Add system-gsl-version.patch relaxing the GSL version gate so system
  ms-gsl 5.x is accepted (fixes a configure failure that already broke
  1.29.0).
- Add system-cpuinfo.patch restoring the system cpuinfo find upstream
  1.31.0 dropped (same configure failure class).
- Restrict tar_scm tag matching to v* so commits shared with plugin
  releases no longer resolve to plugin tags.
- Apply the onnx patch with upstream's flags (its newer hunks need
  --ignore-whitespace).
- Spec cleanup: spec-cleaner canonical, plain -devel names kept.

